# Biofilm Formation Analysis R Script

This R script analyzes biofilm formation (OD values) across bacterial organisms, metabolite treatments (Sphingosine and Harmane), and concentrations, comparing each treatment against its matched control (DBM for Sphingosine, DM for Harmane).

It reshapes wide-format OD data to long format, parses condition names into organism, treatment, concentration, and type, and produces a boxplot with overlaid jittered points, faceted by organism and colored by compound. It then runs two-tailed Wilcoxon rank-sum tests for each treatment–control pair, reporting medians, IQRs, median difference, Hodges–Lehmann estimate with 95% CI, U statistic, rank-biserial correlation, Cliff's delta, p-value, and significance stars.

## Input

- `joined_biofilm_ODs.csv` — wide-format OD measurements with one row per replicate and one column per condition, using column names like `<Organism>_<S|H>_<concentration>` (treatments) or `<Organism>_<DM|DBM>` (controls).

## Output

- `biofilm_boxplot.svg` — faceted boxplot with jittered points (5×8 in)
- `biofilm_statistics.csv` — full statistical results per comparison
- `biofilm_statistics_condensed.csv` — publication-style condensed table with formatted medians, Δ median [95% CI], effect sizes, and p-values

## Requirements

R with `tidyr`, `dplyr`, `ggplot2`, `ggpubr`, `broom`, `svglite`, and `effsize`.

## Note

Set the working directory and input filename at the top before running.
